Author: Muhammad Mohsin Khan
Created: 9.10.2026
# ==========================================================
# CalculiX GraphiX (cgx) FBD script
# Section 5.1 - Cantilever beam from the CalculiX CrunchiX manual
# Unit system: mm, s, N, tonne
#
# Geometry: 1000 x 1000 x 8000 mm; beam axis is global Z.
# Fixed end: z = 0 mm. Free/load end: z = 8000 mm.
# Reference end force for the CCX input deck: 9.0E6 N.
#
# Mesh: linear hexahedra (HE8/C3D20R), 10 x 10 x 80 divisions.
# Expected nominal mesh: 8000 brick elements.
#
# Run from a writable working directory:
#   cgx -b cantilever_5_1_mm.fbd
#
# The script exports the mesh and named node sets. Depending on the CGX
# version, the Abaqus-format mesh/set files are written using the set names.
# ==========================================================

valu L 8000
valu B 1000
valu H 1000
valu NX 10
valu NY 10
valu NZ 80
valu TOL 0.01

# Create a 1000 mm line along X, then sweep it in Y to create the square
# cross-section, then sweep the cross-section in Z to create the solid.
pnt p1 0 0 0
pnt p2 B 0 0
line lbase p1 p2
div lbase NX
seta base_line l lbase

swep base_line cross_section tra 0 H 0 NY
seta cross_section_surfaces s A001

swep cross_section_surfaces beam tra 0 0 L NZ

# Mesh the swept solid with linear hexahedral elements.
elty all he20r
mesh all

# Select all mesh nodes, then select the two end faces by coordinate.
seta ALL_NODES n all
enq ALL_NODES FIX rec _ _ 0 TOL
enq ALL_NODES LOADEND rec _ _ L TOL

# Export the full mesh and named node sets in Abaqus/CalculiX-compatible
# format. FIX and LOADEND are node sets for *BOUNDARY and *CLOAD usage.
send all abq
send FIX abq nam
send LOADEND abq nam
send ALL_NODES abq nam

# Optional visual checks when running interactively:
# plot e all
# plot n FIX
# plot n LOADEND
